      "solution": "First, let $u=2-3x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u$, solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{2-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|2-3x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
